  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Question": "In \\(\\triangle ABC\\) and \\(\\triangle DEF\\), \\(AB=DE\\), \\(\\angle B=\\angle E\\), and \\(BC=EF\\). Which criterion establishes that they are congruent?",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "SSA",
    "B": "ASA",
    "C": "SAS",
    "D": "AAS"
  },
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "\\(\\angle B\\) is the included angle between \\(AB\\) and \\(BC\\), and \\(\\angle E\\) is the included angle between \\(DE\\) and \\(EF\\). Two sides and their included angle are respectively equal, so the criterion is SAS.",
